Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Achieving Hyperbolicity by Direct Ensemble Averaging", "Subchapter",ExpressionUUID->"7e759eb1-b614-4331-b05e-b3bf9d3d7c3c"],

Cell["\<\
The stochastic gradients so far all evaluate a single closed-form \
transmittance function at a sampled distance -- correct, but it leans on the \
closed-form integral already having been solved. A more direct demonstration \
skips the closed form entirely: draw a genuinely fresh, independent \[Sigma] \
from its own exponential distribution for every single trial, evaluate Exp[-\
\[Sigma] s] for that trial\[CloseCurlyQuote]s own \[Sigma], and average \
directly over many such trials. If the earlier derivation is right, this \
brute-force ensemble average should converge to the same hyperbolic curve \
without ever using the closed-form 1/(1+\[Sigma]bar s) expression at all.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6dec53e0-ca40-429b-bd3e-c4a9aca5dc5d"],

Cell["expSample[sig_, rnd_] := -(Log[1 - rnd]/sig)", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[50]:=",ExpressionUUID->"aa7f39b9-b992-4abf-a27e-170641b6948c"],

Cell["\<\
(* was silently assumed to already exist from the separate \
exponential-gradient notebook -- it does not exist here on its own, and was \
never actually defined in this file until now. That missing definition is the \
real cause of the hang: sigmaDraw called an undefined function, producing \
unevaluated symbolic expressions across the whole grid instead of numbers. *)\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[51]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5571b94b-783e-4d41-b34e-da5c491ff896"],

Cell["sigmaDraw[sigmabar_] := expSample[1/sigmabar, RandomReal[]]", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[52]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2929dc55-0209-45bc-a99e-7bf678e3e2e0"],

Cell["\<\
(* one fresh random rate per call, mean sigmabar, using the exponential \
sampler already defined for the exp-gradient panels *)\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[53]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1a92adff-c2de-42e5-ab43-d4f04fa2cd76"],

Cell["\<\
fMixed[i_, sigmabar_] := Module[{s, trials, d}, s = (i/freq)*20; trials = \
Table[Exp[-sigmaDraw[sigmabar]*s], {nRndSamples}]; d = Mean[trials]; d]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[54]:=",ExpressionUUID->"deb0a4ea-12e4-42dd-a082-81e3c7149437"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Note",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " this is structurally different from f[i,\[Sigma]] above: no \
importance-sampling reweight by a PDF, and no inverse-CDF distance sampling \
at all. \[Sigma] itself is what gets sampled and averaged over here -- \
distance s is simply the fixed point at which we're asking for the \
ensemble-averaged transmittance, mapped linearly from the pixel index."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"51175380-8260-4d9e-9c10-0eb346e2133d"],

Cell["fReference[i_, x0_] := Thyp[(i/freq)*20, x0]", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[55]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a5b30db7-ee19-465d-b2df-64fc02aa8e72"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
GraphicsGrid[{{ MatrixPlot[ParallelTable[fMixed[x, 1.0], {x, freq}, {y, \
freq}], PlotRange -> {0, 1}, ColorFunctionScaling -> fncScaling, Frame -> \
False, ImageSize -> imageSize, PlotLabel -> \"Direct ensemble average over \
random sigma (noisy)\"], MatrixPlot[ParallelTable[fReference[x, 1.0], {x, \
freq}, {y, freq}], PlotRange -> {0, 1}, Frame -> False, ImageSize -> \
imageSize, PlotLabel -> \"Exact hyperbolic curve, same distance convention \
(smooth)\"] }}]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[56]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b3fe6cad-a627-4697-a853-3d767e1579dd"],

